From: CEB-GNRD maintainers <bmc@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] spi-nor: auto-detect CEB-GNRD BIOS only after explicit driver binding

The board BIOS compatible intentionally has no automatic driver match.
The updater selects BMC ownership, sets driver_override and binds spi-nor.
Auto-detect this device by JEDEC ID rather than using the board modalias as
a flash model name. No changes to BMC FMC flash detection.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CEB-GNRD integration]

diff --git a/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/core.c b/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/core.c
--- a/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/core.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/core.c
@@ -3730,7 +3730,8 @@
 	 */
 	if (data && data->type)
 		flash_name = data->type;
-	else if (!strcmp(spi->modalias, "spi-nor"))
+	else if (!strcmp(spi->modalias, "spi-nor") ||
+		 of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "ctopai,ceb-gnrd-host-bios"))
 		flash_name = NULL; /* auto-detect */
 	else
 		flash_name = spi->modalias;
